  "_comment": "Shared console endpoint contract. Both sides assert against this file so drift fails on both CIs: PHP proves each runtime's availability map covers every route-backed key and that its reason map matches (`EndpointCapabilitiesTest` on Laravel, `WP_MCP_AI_REST_Console_Endpoints_Test` on WordPress), and Vitest proves the console builds exactly those keys (`runtime-config.test.ts`). Add a key here first, then wire it. 'asset' keys are build outputs, not routes, so the backend does not report them. 'reasons' is the canonical (Laravel) supply class; 'wordpress_reasons' holds only the keys whose class differs on WordPress — merge it over 'reasons' for that runtime. 'reason_codes' is the shared vocabulary: only reason 'route' is meant to be served, so a false 'route' key is a gap. 'not-installed' is applied at runtime when a Pro-supplied route's addon is inactive. 'fragments' is the golden route fragment each runtime must register for the key.",
